evotion by day, and at night His song is with me as a prayer to the God of my life.","verse":8}],"id":"Lord","label":"LORD","matchReviews":[{"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","scope":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","senseReview":"Only literal uppercase LORD is admitted globally. Source Lord article explicitly covers God as Lord; lowercase human lord and sentence-title Lord are not inferred from this rule.","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord","term":"LORD"}],"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","matchingRules":["reviewed_exact_headword"],"sourceProvenanceId":"Lord","sourceTitle":"Lord"},{"evidence":[{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"Savior","senseEvidence":{"basis":"source_verse_citation","originalCitations":[{"anchorIndex":10,"href":"?bref=Ps.42.5,11","rawReference":"Ps.42.5,11"}],"ruleId":"Savior::Savior::source_verse_citation","sourceHeadwordId":"Savior"},"text":"Why are you downcast, O my soul? Why the unease within me? Put your hope in God, for I will yet praise Him, my Savior and my God.","verse":11}],"id":"Savior","label":"Savior","matchReviews":[{"ruleId":"Savior::Savior::source_verse_citation","scope":"source_verse_citation","senseReview":"Reviewed original headword and source sense. This substantive word is admitted only where the original article explicitly cites the exact occurrence verse; ambiguous homographs and known context mismatches are separately excluded. This is selective contextual evidence, not an automatic rule for every same-spelling word.","sourceHeadwordId":"Savior","term":"Savior"}],"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","matchingRules":["reviewed_exact_headword"],"sourceProvenanceId":"Savior","sourceTitle":"Savior"}],"format":"bsb-study-chapter-v2","notes":[{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":["Questions and Doubt"],"sourceClass":"theme-title","t":"h"},{"c":["The psalmists are not afraid to ask questions and express doubts. The number of questions in a psalm indicates the intensity of the mood or the significance of the issue at hand. The psalms with the greatest number of questions raise the important issues of God’s perceived abandonment (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.13.1-6","r":"Ps.13.1-6","rawR":"Ps.13.1-6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.13.1-6","value":"Ps.13.1-6"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ps 13"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.42.1-43.5","r":"Ps.42.1-43.5","rawR":"Ps.42.1-43.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.42.1-43.5","value":"Ps.42.1-43.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"Pss 42–43"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.74.1-23","r":"Ps.74.1-23","rawR":"Ps.74.1-23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.74.1-23","value":"Ps.74.1-23"}],"t":"ref","v":"74"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.89.1-52","r":"Ps.89.1-52","rawR":"Ps.89.1-52","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.89.1-52","value":"Ps.89.1-52"}],"t":"ref","v":"89"},") and the prosperity of the wicked (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.73.1-28","r":"Ps.73.1-28","rawR":"Ps.73.1-28","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.73.1-28","value":"Ps.73.1-28"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ps 73"},")."],"sourceClass":"theme-body-fl","t":"p"},{"c":["The psalmists’ questions clarify life issues. Some questions ask whether the Lord is the true God (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.94.9-10","r":"Ps.94.9-10","rawR":"Ps.94.9-10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.94.9-10","value":"Ps.94.9-10"}],"t":"ref","v":"94:9-10"},") and why he seems to have abandoned the godly (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.77.7","r":"Ps.77.7","rawR":"Ps.77.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.77.7","value":"Ps.77.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"77:7"},"). Other questions call attention to the success of the wicked (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.10.13","r":"Ps.10.13","rawR":"Ps.10.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.10.13","value":"Ps.10.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"10:13"},"), the impotence of the godly (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.11.3","r":"Ps.11.3","rawR":"Ps.11.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.11.3","value":"Ps.11.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"11:3"},"), the election of Zion (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.68.16","r":"Ps.68.16","rawR":"Ps.68.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.68.16","value":"Ps.68.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"68:16"},"), the power of God (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.114.5-6","r":"Ps.114.5-6","rawR":"Ps.114.5-6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.114.5-6","value":"Ps.114.5-6"}],"t":"ref","v":"114:5-6"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.147.17","r":"Ps.147.17","rawR":"Ps.147.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.147.17","value":"Ps.147.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"147:17"},"), the folly of the nations (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.2.1","r":"Ps.2.1","rawR":"Ps.2.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.2.1","value":"Ps.2.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"2:1"},"), and the issue of injustice (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.82.2","r":"Ps.82.2","rawR":"Ps.82.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.82.2","value":"Ps.82.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"82:2"},"). The psalmists question, examine, challenge, doubt, and occasionally despair over God’s seeming lack of concern."],"sourceClass":"theme-body","t":"p"},{"c":["The psalmists’ questions may also lead to praise and worship: “Who can list the glorious miracles of the ",{"c":["Lord"],"sourceClass":"divine-name","t":"span"},"? Who can ever praise him enough?” (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.106.2","r":"Ps.106.2","rawR":"Ps.106.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.106.2","value":"Ps.106.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"106:2"},"). The question, “Who will come from Mount Zion to rescue Israel?” (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.53.6","r":"Ps.53.6","rawR":"Ps.53.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.53.6","value":"Ps.53.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"53:6"},") calls attention to the answer: The Lord rescues his people. For many questions, the implied answer brings praise to the Lord: “Whom have I in heaven but you? I desire you more than anything on earth” (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.73.25","r":"Ps.73.25","rawR":"Ps.73.25","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.73.25","value":"Ps.73.25"}],"t":"ref","v":"73:25"},"; see also ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.89.8","r":"Ps.89.8","rawR":"Ps.89.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.89.8","value":"Ps.89.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"89:8"},"). Questions may also express wonder at God’s grace (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.8.4","r":"Ps.8.4","rawR":"Ps.8.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.8.4","value":"Ps.8.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"8:4"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.130.3","r":"Ps.130.3","rawR":"Ps.130.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.130.3","value":"Ps.130.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"130:3"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.144.3","r":"Ps.144.3","rawR":"Ps.144.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.144.3","value":"Ps.144.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"144:3"},")."],"sourceClass":"theme-body","t":"p"},{"c":["Asking good questions can be the beginning of a dialogue with the Lord that leads us along the path of wisdom and results in worship and praise."],"sourceClass":"theme-body","t":"p"},{"c":["Passages for Further Study"],"sourceClass":"theme-refs-title","t":"h"},{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.2.1","r":"Ps.2.1","rawR":"Ps.2.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.2.1","value":"Ps.2.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Pss 2:1"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.4.2","r":"Ps.4.2","rawR":"Ps.4.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.4.2","value":"Ps.4.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"4:2"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.6.3","r":"Ps.6.3","rawR":"Ps.6.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.6.3","value":"Ps.6.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"6:3"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.10.1","r":"Ps.10.1","rawR":"Ps.10.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.10.1","value":"Ps.10.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"10:1"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.11.3","r":"Ps.11.3","rawR":"Ps.11.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.11.3","value":"Ps.11.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"11:3"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.13.1-6","r":"Ps.13.1-6","rawR":"Ps.13.1-6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.13.1-6","value":"Ps.13.1-6"}],"t":"ref","v":"13:1-6"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.22.1","r":"Ps.22.1","rawR":"Ps.22.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.22.1","value":"Ps.22.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"22:1"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.35.17","r":"Ps.35.17","rawR":"Ps.35.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.35.17","value":"Ps.35.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"35:17"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.42.1-11","r":"Ps.42.1-11","rawR":"Ps.42.1-11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.42.1-11","value":"Ps.42.1-11"}],"t":"ref","v":"42:1-11"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.43.1-5","r":"Ps.43.1-5","rawR":"Ps.43.1-5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.43.1-5","value":"Ps.43.1-5"}],"t":"ref","v":"43:1-5"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.44.23-24","r":"Ps.44.23-24","rawR":"Ps.44.23-24","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.44.23-24","value":"Ps.44.23-24"}],"t":"ref","v":"44:23-24"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.53.6","r":"Ps.53.6","rawR":"Ps.53.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.53.6","value":"Ps.53.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"53:6"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.60.9-10","r":"Ps.60.9-10","rawR":"Ps.60.9-10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.60.9-10","value":"Ps.60.9-10"}],"t":"ref","v":"60:9-10"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.68.16","r":"Ps.68.16","rawR":"Ps.68.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.68.16","value":"Ps.68.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"68:16"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.73.1-74.23","r":"Ps.73.1-74.23","rawR":"Ps.73.1-74.23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.73.1-74.23","value":"Ps.73.1-74.23"}],"t":"ref","v":"73:1–74:23"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.77.8-9","r":"Ps.77.8-9","rawR":"Ps.77.8-9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.77.8-9","value":"Ps.77.8-9"}],"t":"ref","v":"77:8-9"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.79.5","r":"Ps.79.5","rawR":"Ps.79.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.79.5","value":"Ps.79.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"79:5"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.80.4","r":"Ps.80.4","rawR":"Ps.80.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.80.4","value":"Ps.80.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"80:4"},", ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.80.12","r":"Ps.80.12","rawR":"Ps.80.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.80.12","value":"Ps.80.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"12"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.82.2","r":"Ps.82.2","rawR":"Ps.82.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.82.2","value":"Ps.82.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"82:2"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.83.2","r":"Ps.83.2","rawR":"Ps.83.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.83.2","value":"Ps.83.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"83:2"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.85.5-6","r":"Ps.85.5-6","rawR":"Ps.85.5-6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.85.5-6","value":"Ps.85.5-6"}],"t":"ref","v":"85:5-6"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.88.14","r":"Ps.88.14","rawR":"Ps.88.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.88.14","value":"Ps.88.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"88:14"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.89.1-52","r":"Ps.89.1-52","rawR":"Ps.89.1-52","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.89.1-52","value":"Ps.89.1-52"}],"t":"ref","v":"89:1-52"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.90.11","r":"Ps.90.11","rawR":"Ps.90.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.90.11","value":"Ps.90.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"90:11"},", ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.90.13","r":"Ps.90.13","rawR":"Ps.90.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.90.13","value":"Ps.90.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"13"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.94.3-4","r":"Ps.94.3-4","rawR":"Ps.94.3-4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.94.3-4","value":"Ps.94.3-4"}],"t":"ref","v":"94:3-4"},", ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.94.16","r":"Ps.94.16","rawR":"Ps.94.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.94.16","value":"Ps.94.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"16"},", ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.94.20","r":"Ps.94.20","rawR":"Ps.94.20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.94.20","value":"Ps.94.20"}],"t":"ref","v":"20"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.101.2","r":"Ps.101.2","rawR":"Ps.101.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.101.2","value":"Ps.101.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"101:2"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.108.10-11","r":"Ps.108.10-11","rawR":"Ps.108.10-11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.108.10-11","value":"Ps.108.10-11"}],"t":"ref","v":"108:10-11"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.114.5-6","r":"Ps.114.5-6","rawR":"Ps.114.5-6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.114.5-6","value":"Ps.114.5-6"}],"t":"ref","v":"114:5-6"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.119.82","r":"Ps.119.82","rawR":"Ps.119.82","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.119.82","value":"Ps.119.82"}],"t":"ref","v":"119:82"},", ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.119.84","r":"Ps.119.84","rawR":"Ps.119.84","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.119.84","value":"Ps.119.84"}],"t":"ref","v":"84"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.137.4","r":"Ps.137.4","rawR":"Ps.137.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.137.4","value":"Ps.137.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"137:4"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.147.17","r":"Ps.147.17","rawR":"Ps.147.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.147.17","value":"Ps.147.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"147:17"}],"sourceClass":"theme-refs","t":"p"}],"id":"ThemeNote:QuestionsAndDoubt","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":43,"endVerse":5,"startChapter":42,"startVerse":1}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"QuestionsAndDoubt","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"ThemeNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[42,43],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"4cc402bfb5426b8acb8d22e25dcf5bbf7b76fa4d86c4b93f7339f688b370e306","sourceItemName":"QuestionsAndDoubt","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/ThemeNotes.xml","sourceOrder":114,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.42.1-43.5","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":"Questions and Doubt","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Questions and Doubt","type":"ThemeNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.42.1-43.5","r":"Ps.42.1-43.5","rawR":"Ps.42.1-43.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.42.1-43.5","value":"Ps.42.1-43.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"Pss 42–43"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," These psalms, like ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.9.1-20","r":"Ps.9.1-20","rawR":"Ps.9.1-20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.9.1-20","value":"Ps.9.1-20"}],"t":"ref","v":"Pss 9"}," and ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.10.1-18","r":"Ps.10.1-18","rawR":"Ps.10.1-18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.10.1-18","value":"Ps.10.1-18"}],"t":"ref","v":"10"},", form a unit comprising a lament with a bittersweet refrain of hope (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.42.5","r":"Ps.42.5","rawR":"Ps.42.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.42.5","value":"Ps.42.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"42:5"},", ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.42.11","r":"Ps.42.11","rawR":"Ps.42.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.42.11","value":"Ps.42.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"11"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.43.5","r":"Ps.43.5","rawR":"Ps.43.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.43.5","value":"Ps.43.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"43:5"},"). In many Hebrew manuscripts these two psalms are combined as one. The historical context is uncertain; these psalms might be the voice of God’s people in exile, confessing their loyalty to God as he punishes them for their prevailing apostasy. The psalmist longs for fellowship with God such as he enjoyed in Jerusalem (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.42.4","r":"Ps.42.4","rawR":"Ps.42.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.42.4","value":"Ps.42.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"42:4"},"); his memories only make him more discouraged. As the psalmist cries out to God, he recalls God’s love and faithfulness (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.42.8","r":"Ps.42.8","rawR":"Ps.42.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.42.8","value":"Ps.42.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"42:8"},"), which moves him to plead for vindication (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.43.1-4","r":"Ps.43.1-4","rawR":"Ps.43.1-4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.43.1-4","value":"Ps.43.1-4"}],"t":"ref","v":"43:1-4"},")."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.42.1-43.5","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":43,"endVerse":5,"startChapter":42,"startVerse":1}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.42.1-43.5","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[42,43],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"2cc37f14c4c4fe9a768dd53b0f3dc76e8585d7ee7a255fdef0e62a9f86cb640a","sourceItemName":"Ps.42.1-43.5","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":6425,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.42.1-43.5","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.42.1-43.5","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.42.1","r":"Ps.42.1","rawR":"Ps.42.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.42.1","value":"Ps.42.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"42:title"}," ",{"c":["The descendants of Korah"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," were members of a Levitical choir appointed by David to serve as Temple singers (see ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.6.22-38","r":"1Chr.6.22-38","rawR":"1Chr.6.22-38","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.6.22-38","value":"1Chr.6.22-38"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 6:22-38"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.9.19-34","r":"1Chr.9.19-34","rawR":"1Chr.9.19-34","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.9.19-34","value":"1Chr.9.19-34"}],"t":"ref","v":"9:19-34"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.20.19","r":"2Chr.20.19","rawR":"2Chr.20.19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.20.19","value":"2Chr.20.19"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 20:19"},"). Their ancestor Korah was the apostate who had rebelled against Moses and whom the earth swallowed up (",{"href":"?bref=Exod.6.24","r":"Exod.6.24","rawR":"Exod.6.24","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.6.24","value":"Exod.6.24"}],"t":"ref","v":"Exod 6:24"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Num.16.1-50","r":"Num.16.1-50","rawR":"Num.16.1-50","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.16.1-50","value":"Num.16.1-50"}],"t":"ref","v":"Num 16"},")."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.42.1","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":42,"endVerse":1,"startChapter":42,"startVerse":1}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.42.1","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[42],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"de22121b5975884d9734a9f4621f734711e9d03005738363b04f18b02273c228","sourceItemName":"Ps.42.1","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":6426,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.42.1","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.42.1","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.42.1-4","r":"Ps.42.1-4","rawR":"Ps.42.1-4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.42.1-4","value":"Ps.42.1-4"}],"t":"ref","v":"42:1-4"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," The psalmist’s longing for God comes from being geographically distant from the Temple as he remembers the past. • The verb translated ",{"c":["longs"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," is found only here and in ",{"href":"?bref=Joel.1.20","r":"Joel.1.20","rawR":"Joel.1.20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Joel.1.20","value":"Joel.1.20"}],"t":"ref","v":"Joel 1:20"}," (“cry out”); in both cases it refers to extreme ",{"c":["thirst"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," in a waterless desert (see ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.63.1","r":"Ps.63.1","rawR":"Ps.63.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.63.1","value":"Ps.63.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Pss 63:1"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.143.6","r":"Ps.143.6","rawR":"Ps.143.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.143.6","value":"Ps.143.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"143:6"},"; see also ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.84.2","r":"Ps.84.2","rawR":"Ps.84.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.84.2","value":"Ps.84.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"84:2"},")."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.42.1-4","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":42,"endVerse":4,"startChapter":42,"startVerse":1}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.42.1-4","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[42],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"546522447f16fbb6f42393781dab2b88ffd2e6d2f37e571817485b1bb754964a","sourceItemName":"Ps.42.1-4","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":6427,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.42.1-4","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.42.1-4","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.42.3","r":"Ps.42.3","rawR":"Ps.42.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.42.3","value":"Ps.42.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"42:3"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," Having ",{"c":["tears for food"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," speaks of great grief (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.80.5","r":"Ps.80.5","rawR":"Ps.80.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.80.5","value":"Ps.80.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"80:5"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.102.9","r":"Ps.102.9","rawR":"Ps.102.9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.102.9","value":"Ps.102.9"}],"t":"ref","v":"102:9"},"; see ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.6.6","r":"Ps.6.6","rawR":"Ps.6.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.6.6","value":"Ps.6.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"6:6"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.56.8","r":"Ps.56.8","rawR":"Ps.56.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.56.8","value":"Ps.56.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"56:8"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.119.136","r":"Ps.119.136","rawR":"Ps.119.136","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.119.136","value":"Ps.119.136"}],"t":"ref","v":"119:136"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.126.5","r":"Ps.126.5","rawR":"Ps.126.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.126.5","value":"Ps.126.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"126:5"},"). • The wicked try to hold God to their timetable and deny his power to intervene."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.42.3","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":42,"endVerse":3,"startChapter":42,"startVerse":3}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.42.3","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[42],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"2cfe77807c7218132baa7d89504da7bc5f039af47ca8f0be133d219845f6d768","sourceItemName":"Ps.42.3","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":6428,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.42.3","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.42.3","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.42.4","r":"Ps.42.4","rawR":"Ps.42.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.42.4","value":"Ps.42.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"42:4"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," The psalmist recalls ",{"c":["leading a great procession"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," as a member of the Levitical choir, possibly during the high holy days."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.42.4","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":42,"endVerse":4,"startChapter":42,"startVerse":4}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.42.4","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[42],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"3d2d042e9b4b529121756479798a5fd331f2df3c09017e67f140db1dfc2acac4","sourceItemName":"Ps.42.4","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":6429,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.42.4","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.42.4","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.42.5-6","r":"Ps.42.5-6","rawR":"Ps.42.5-6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.42.5-6","value":"Ps.42.5-6"}],"t":"ref","v":"42:5-6"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," The psalmist encourages himself with questions and answers."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.42.5-6","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":42,"endVerse":6,"startChapter":42,"startVerse":5}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.42.5-6","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[42],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"c707649128b81bf7cf51e0c84adf51700c02f29606527bb9c7b444316f585b2a","sourceItemName":"Ps.42.5-6","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":6430,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.42.5-6","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.42.5-6","typ